        "Abstract": "This paper presents a method to construct a large-scale, high-quality Japanese web corpus for training Japanese Large Language Models (LLMs). The corpus is built by extracting and refining text from the Common Crawl archive, resulting in approximately 312.1 billion characters. The quality of the corpus is confirmed through continual pre-training on various base LLMs, achieving consistent improvements on Japanese benchmark datasets."
